    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Nut recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Sweden|Swedish Cuisine]]\n\n'''Brända mandlar''' (literally \"burnt almonds\") is a recipe for Swedish candied [[Cookbook:Almond|almond]]s.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 100 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[cookbook:Almond|blanched almonds]]\n* 100 g [[cookbook:Powdered Sugar|icing sugar]]\n* 125 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[cookbook:water|water]]\n* 1 drop red [[Cookbook:Food Coloring|food colouring]] (optional)\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Put the almonds in the oven at 180 °C for a few minutes to toast them.\n#Pour the water into a heavy-bottomed [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]], then sprinkle in the sugar. Place over a low heat, and stir until the mixture thickens.\n#Add the colouring. Stir in the almonds so that they get a nice coating.\n#Spread out the almonds on some [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|baking paper]], separate the almonds using a fork, and let them cool a bit.\n\n[[Category:Swedish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes for confections]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using powdered sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using food coloring]]",
